Krita Nova 72 - Transform tool: a floating actions bar

While the Transform tool is active, a small bar floats over the canvas,
drawn as the selection actions bar is (30 px buttons side by side with
24 px icons, its outlines and background, its drag handle): Flip Horizontally, Flip Vertically,
Rotate 90° counter-clockwise and clockwise (these four in Free Transform
mode), Reset the transform, the transform mode (a menu: Free, Perspective,
Warp, Cage, Liquify, Mesh; the button shows the current one), Cancel and
Apply. Like the selection actions bar, it sticks to what is being transformed:
centered 30 px under the transformed area, following it as it is moved,
scaled or rotated and as the view is zoomed or panned (on the canvas
always). Its grip (the dots at its right end) moves it away from there, and
that offset is remembered (kritarc [KisToolTransform]
novaTransformBarOffsetFromArea). With no transform running it waits at the
bottom middle of the canvas. Pen, touch and mouse work on it.
(plugins/tools/tool_transform2/kis_transform_actions_bar.*)

